  "step_2": "The individual reflects on the likelihood of losing money in each option. They note that in Option B, they would 'very likely' lose either 4000 or 2000 Euros. They emphasize that in Option A, there is a 75% chance (they say 72%, likely a rounding or verbal approximation) of making no loss. They mention that the 25% chance of losing more in A is weighed against the smaller losses in B, suggesting a trade-off between probability and loss magnitude. The individual focuses on the probability of avoiding loss and compares the risk profiles, particularly the higher chance of no loss in A versus more frequent but smaller losses in B. Their justification centers on probability and outcome severity trade-offs, not on whether any outcome is certain.",
